---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "@/components/Code.astro";
import { withBase } from "@/lib/utils";
const snippet0 = `from power_pptx import Presentation

prs = Presentation("deck.pptx")
paths = prs.render_thumbnails(out_dir="thumbs")    # every slide -> PNG, 150 dpi
[p.name for p in paths]
# ['_render_input-page-1.png', '_render_input-page-2.png', '_render_input-page-3.png']

prs.render_thumbnails(out_dir="small", dpi=72)     # a 10" slide is 720 px wide
png = prs.slides[0].render_thumbnail(return_bytes=True)   # one slide, as bytes`;

const snippet1 = `from power_pptx.render import render_slides

# Selected slides with a name template (the index counts from 0)
render_slides(
    prs,
    slides=[0, 1, 2],
    out_dir="thumbs",
    name_template="slide-{:02d}.png",
    scale=2,                      # 144 dpi; overrides dpi=
    font_dirs=["assets/fonts"],   # fonts LibreOffice should see
)`;

const snippet2 = `from power_pptx.render import ThumbnailRendererError, ThumbnailRendererUnavailable

try:
    prs.render_thumbnails(out_dir="thumbs", timeout=60)
except ThumbnailRendererUnavailable:
    ...   # no soffice / libreoffice to run
except ThumbnailRendererError as exc:
    ...   # LibreOffice failed, timed out, or there is no way to split the PDF`;

---

<DocsLayout
  title="Rendering Thumbnails"
  description="Render slides to PNG via LibreOffice — for previews, agent feedback loops and CI visual diffs."
>
  <p class="lead">
    The thumbnail renderer shells out to LibreOffice (<code>soffice</code>) to produce PNG previews
    of slides — handy for agent feedback loops, CI visual diffs, or gallery pages like this one.
  </p>

  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>soffice</code> (LibreOffice) on <code>PATH</code> — or <code>libreoffice</code>, or a
      binary named by <code>soffice_bin=</code> or <code>POWER_PPTX_SOFFICE</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>pdftoppm</code> (Poppler) <em>or</em> <code>pypdfium2</code>
      (<code>pip install 'power-pptx[review]'</code>) to split the rendered PDF into slides
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Without LibreOffice you get <code>ThumbnailRendererUnavailable</code> — catch it to degrade
    gracefully. Without a PDF splitter only a one-slide deck can be rendered, through
    LibreOffice's PNG filter; a longer deck raises <code>ThumbnailRendererError</code> saying what
    to install.
  </p>

  <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
  <Code code={snippet0} />
  <Code code={snippet1} />
  <p>
    Rendering goes through PDF: LibreOffice exports the deck, and each page is rasterised at
    <code>dpi</code> (150 by default) — for every deck, one-slide decks included.
    <code>render_slides(scale=...)</code> is the same knob in PDF units, <code>1.0</code> being 72
    dpi. Files are named <code>_render_input-page-N.png</code>, <code>N</code> counting from 1 and
    zero-padded to the width of the slide count; pass <code>name_template</code> to
    <code>render_slides</code> for names of your own. Hidden slides are rendered like any other, so
    <code>slide_indexes=[n]</code> (or <code>slides=[n]</code>) always means
    <code>prs.slides[n]</code>; that needs LibreOffice 7.4 or later.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each call uses a private workspace and LibreOffice profile. Reusing <code>out_dir</code>
    returns only the current render's requested slides, even when the deck gets shorter.
    Unrelated files are preserved; matching output filenames are replaced. Intermediate
    files are cleaned up, and <code>return_bytes=True</code> does not write output files.
    Folders registered with <code>power_pptx.text.register_font_dir</code> are always handed to
    LibreOffice, so previews use the real typeface rather than a fallback.
  </p>

  <h2 id="errors">Errors and timeouts</h2>
  <Code code={snippet2} />
  <p>
    <code>timeout=</code> (seconds, default 120) applies to the LibreOffice conversion and to the
    PDF split separately. A step that overruns is stopped together with every process LibreOffice
    started, and <code>ThumbnailRendererError</code> is raised.
  </p>

  <h2 id="agent-loop">The agent feedback loop</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Agent generates the deck and calls <code>slide.tidy()</code>.</li>
    <li><code>render_thumbnails()</code> produces PNGs of the result.</li>
    <li>The agent (or a human) inspects the thumbnails and iterates.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Combined with <code>audit(prs).markdown()</code>, this closes the loop between generation and
    verification without ever opening PowerPoint. For a complete bundle — PDF, every PNG, contact
    sheets, validation and a gallery — use <code>power-pptx review</code>; see
    <a href={`${withBase("/advanced/authoring-workflows")}#review`}>Modern Authoring Workflows</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
